USAGE: retriever jira <subcommand> [options]

Jira Cloud commands

SUBCOMMANDS:
  export    export one Jira document as a Markdown file in the --out folder
  whoami    show the Jira account that the source's credentials sign in as
  projects  Jira projects commands
  issues    Jira issues commands
  comments  Jira comments commands

OPTIONS:
  -h, --help  show help

EXIT STATUS:
  0    the command completed
  2    the command did not complete: a usage mistake, a configuration error, or a failed request
  124  a bounded wait elapsed before the command finished; the failure is retryable
  125  the environment refused before the command started, such as a port already in use

USAGE: retriever jira whoami [--source <id>]

show the Jira account that the source's credentials sign in as

OPTIONS:
  --source <id>  configured source ID; required when more than one jira source exists
  -h, --help     show help

EXIT STATUS:
  0    the command completed
  2    the command did not complete: a usage mistake, a configuration error, or a failed request
  124  a bounded wait elapsed before the command finished; the failure is retryable
  125  the environment refused before the command started, such as a port already in use

USAGE: retriever jira projects list [--query <value>] [--limit <n>] [--offset <n>] [--source <id>]

list one page of the Jira projects of a Jira source, which Retriever shows as collections

OPTIONS:
  --query <value>  a text to match against the project names, 1 to 1000 characters
  --limit <n>      the number of projects in the page, from 1 to 50
  --offset <n>     the number of projects to skip
  --source <id>    configured source ID; required when more than one jira source exists
  -h, --help       show help

EXIT STATUS:
  0    the command completed
  2    the command did not complete: a usage mistake, a configuration error, or a failed request
  124  a bounded wait elapsed before the command finished; the failure is retryable
  125  the environment refused before the command started, such as a port already in use

USAGE: retriever jira issues search <jql> [--limit <n>] [--source <id>]

search the Jira issues that match a JQL query, one page of at most 100 issues

ARGUMENTS:
  <jql>

OPTIONS:
  --limit <n>    the number of issues to show, from 1 to 100
  --source <id>  configured source ID; required when more than one jira source exists
  -h, --help     show help

EXIT STATUS:
  0    the command completed
  2    the command did not complete: a usage mistake, a configuration error, or a failed request
  124  a bounded wait elapsed before the command finished; the failure is retryable
  125  the environment refused before the command started, such as a port already in use

USAGE: retriever jira issues get <issueKey> [--source <id>]

print the Markdown of one Jira issue

ARGUMENTS:
  <issueKey>

OPTIONS:
  --source <id>  configured source ID; required when more than one jira source exists
  -h, --help     show help

EXIT STATUS:
  0    the command completed
  2    the command did not complete: a usage mistake, a configuration error, or a failed request
  124  a bounded wait elapsed before the command finished; the failure is retryable
  125  the environment refused before the command started, such as a port already in use

USAGE: retriever jira comments list <issueKey> [--limit <n>] [--offset <n>] [--source <id>]

list one page of the comments of one Jira issue, as Markdown

ARGUMENTS:
  <issueKey>

OPTIONS:
  --limit <n>    the number of comments in the page, from 1 to 100
  --offset <n>   the number of comments to skip
  --source <id>  configured source ID; required when more than one jira source exists
  -h, --help     show help

EXIT STATUS:
  0    the command completed
  2    the command did not complete: a usage mistake, a configuration error, or a failed request
  124  a bounded wait elapsed before the command finished; the failure is retryable
  125  the environment refused before the command started, such as a port already in use
